description:
Start a flag release: release a flag across environments, by following a flag release plan (kind "plan") or by listing the environments (kind "custom"). Beta API. When the user names no project, call get-projects before you ask anything: when it returns one project, name that project in the confirmation question. This changes the flag's targeting as the release runs, so confirm the project, the flag, the plan or the environments, and how each environment releases with the user first. When the user did not name the project, name the one you picked and wait for their reply before you send confirm: true. A flag can have only one active release; if it already has one, LaunchDarkly returns an error that names it, and that release must be archived first. With kind "plan", flagReleasePlanKey names the plan (find one with get-flag-release-plans; use the plan with default: true unless the user picks another). Use kind "custom" when the project has no flag release plan, or when the release the user asks for does not fit a plan: environments lists each environment in release order, in the shape create-automated-rollout-config takes. An immediate environment is only environmentKey: releaseType is only override or policy, never immediate. startingVariationId and endingVariationId name the variations to release from and to, by the _id of the flag's variations. Send both or neither: a multi-variate flag needs both, and a boolean flag can omit both to release from false to true. Send pullRequest when the release is for a pull request: repoFullName as owner/name and number; the tool sends the github.com pull request URL built from them. A webhook environment in a release with a pull request waits for a deploy that includes the merge. Without a pull request, it starts on the next deploy signal for that environment. Returns config_id, the release's ID, and the release as read back, with repo_full_name and pr_number when a pull request is linked; inspect or change it later with get-automated-rollout-config, update-automated-rollout-config, and archive-automated-rollout-config.
Examples:
- plan, boolean flag, no pull request: {"projectKey":"default","flagKey":"new-checkout","kind":"plan","flagReleasePlanKey":"standard","confirm":true}
- plan, multi-variate flag for a pull request: {"projectKey":"default","flagKey":"checkout-theme","kind":"plan","flagReleasePlanKey":"standard","startingVariationId":"<_id to release from>","endingVariationId":"<_id to release to>","pullRequest":{"repoFullName":"acme/web","number":42},"confirm":true}
- custom, staging immediate and then production with its default environment release plan: {"projectKey":"default","flagKey":"new-checkout","kind":"custom","environments":[{"environmentKey":"staging"},{"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"policy"}],"confirm":true}

environments.description:
Only with kind custom, and required there: each environment, in release order. One example entry per release type. Omit triggerType unless the user says when the release starts.
- immediate: {"environmentKey":"production"}
- progressive: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"override","override":{"releaseMethod":"progressive","rolloutContextKindKey":"user","stages":[{"allocation":10000,"durationMillis":3600000},{"allocation":100000,"durationMillis":3600000}]}}
- guarded: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"override","override":{"releaseMethod":"guarded","rolloutContextKindKey":"user","stages":[{"allocation":10000,"durationMillis":3600000}],"metricKeys":["error-rate"],"rollbackOnRegression":true}}
- policy with a named environment release plan, which always needs releaseType policy: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"policy","environmentReleasePlanKey":"prod-ramp"}

Per-environment rollout plan. One example entry per release type. Omit triggerType unless the user says when the release starts.
- immediate: {"environmentKey":"production"}
- progressive: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"override","override":{"releaseMethod":"progressive","rolloutContextKindKey":"user","stages":[{"allocation":10000,"durationMillis":3600000},{"allocation":100000,"durationMillis":3600000}]}}
- guarded: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"override","override":{"releaseMethod":"guarded","rolloutContextKindKey":"user","stages":[{"allocation":10000,"durationMillis":3600000}],"metricKeys":["error-rate"],"rollbackOnRegression":true}}
- policy with a named environment release plan, which always needs releaseType policy: {"environmentKey":"production","releaseType":"policy","environmentReleasePlanKey":"prod-ramp"}

description:
Update a flag release plan's name, description, maintainer, executionMode, applicationKeys, default, or environments. Beta API. Send only the fields to change; omitted fields keep their current values, including default. environments and applicationKeys are each replaced wholesale when provided, so include every entry to keep. default: true makes this plan the project's default and demotes the current one; default: false unsets this plan as the default and keeps the plan, so the project has no default until another plan is set. To delete a plan, use delete-flag-release-plan. The update is checked against the version that was read, so a concurrent edit returns an error instead of being overwritten; retry to apply it to the current plan. Flag releases already started from the plan are not affected. RULES: 1-50 environments, each listed once, in release order. Each environment needs environmentKey and triggerType, plus environmentReleasePlanKey unless isImmediate is true (never both). The environment release plan must already exist in that environment, be complete, and have exactly one phase; find one with get-environment-release-plans. triggerType: flag_eval starts when the flag is first evaluated there, webhook waits for a deploy signal, manual waits for a person, promotion starts when the previous environment finishes. The first environment cannot use promotion. executionMode is sequential: environments release in the listed order. At most 25 applicationKeys. A project holds at most 100 flag release plans and at most one default.
One example environments entry per trigger for an environment release plan:
- environment release plan, on a CI/CD deploy: {"environmentKey":"staging","triggerType":"webhook","environmentReleasePlanKey":"staging-ramp"}
- environment release plan, when a person starts it: {"environmentKey":"production","triggerType":"manual","environmentReleasePlanKey":"prod-guarded"}
- environment release plan, after the previous environment finishes: {"environmentKey":"production","triggerType":"promotion","environmentReleasePlanKey":"prod-ramp"}
Returns the plan as read back after the update.

environments.description:
